From a77206deb05f6d4ae695e7868586bac62cb94bf2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: scholzri <33288574+scholzri@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 11:17:32 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] zmk: start BLE advertising from the workqueue after settings
 load

zmk_ble_ready() runs from the "ble" settings commit handler, i.e. inside
settings_load() with the settings lock held, and started advertising
there. bt_le_adv_start() sends synchronous HCI commands, which the
Zephyr host transmits from the system workqueue.

With CONFIG_BT_PRIVACY the host generates an IRK when none is stored
yet and, in its own (earlier) commit handler, queues storing the
identity and the IRK on the system workqueue. Those work items block on
the settings lock, so the workqueue never transmits LE Set Random
Address, the command times out after 10 s and BT_ASSERT oopses. On a
board whose fatal handler reboots (MCUboot test image) the image is
never confirmed and reverted, so privacy appears to "not work": the
previous image keeps advertising the public address. Every boot
regenerates the IRK (it was never stored), so it never recovers.

Submit update_advertising_work instead: it runs on the workqueue after
the pending stores, which proceed once settings_load() has returned.
ZMK already starts advertising from this work item after a disconnect.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 app/src/ble.c | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/app/src/ble.c b/app/src/ble.c
index 51b172b9..2a59f95a 100644
--- a/app/src/ble.c
+++ b/app/src/ble.c
@@ -686,7 +686,13 @@ static void zmk_ble_ready(int err) {
         return;
     }
 
-    update_advertising();
+    // Called from the settings commit handler, i.e. while settings_load() holds the settings
+    // lock. Starting advertising here sends synchronous HCI commands, which the host transmits
+    // from the system workqueue. With CONFIG_BT_PRIVACY the host has just queued storing the
+    // freshly generated IRK on that same workqueue, and that work blocks on the settings lock:
+    // a deadlock until the HCI command timeout asserts. Start advertising from the workqueue
+    // instead, after the pending settings stores.
+    k_work_submit(&update_advertising_work);
 }
 
 static int zmk_ble_complete_startup(void) {
-- 
2.53.0

